# Keep the Docker build context small and fast. The hygg-server image only
# needs source + manifests; build artifacts and VCS metadata are excluded.
# NOTE: `docs` must stay IN the context — hygg-server embeds docs/pages/*.md
# at compile time (src/web/docs.rs include_str!), so excluding it breaks the
# build. The include_str! paths point at packages/hygg-server/docs/pages/, which
# is a symlink per page back out to this directory (that indirection is what
# makes the crate publishable — see the comment in src/web/docs.rs), so the
# target has to be in the context or every one of those symlinks dangles here.
# This file also governs what a downstream repo's image build receives when it
# mounts this repo as a named build context.
target
**/target
.git
.github
test-data
assets
data
packages/hygg-server/data
packages/hygg-server/.env
packages/hygg-pwa/dist
packages/hygg-tauri/gen
*.gif
*.png
